    "created_at": "2019-09-08T23:50:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-08T23:50:26Z",
    "body": "> To implement this we would need to cache this data out of process somewhere.\r\n\r\nI think the best place to do this for speed would be an in-memory file  (e.g. on a tmpfs somewhere), but I don't know if there's enough support for this across multiple operating systems to do that (in particular, I have no idea if MacOS/Windows/Termux environments provide enough utilities to do this).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
