    "created_at": "2019-09-08T23:55:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-08T23:55:33Z",
    "body": "Actually, given that starship is (usually) run pretty regularly, the config file should already be in the OS page cache. That means that after the first run in a session, we probably won't see any significant advantage from caching the config file in-memory.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
