    "created_at": "2019-09-09T00:12:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-09T00:12:36Z",
    "body": "I agree that for reading a few small files from the filesystem, we're unlikely to outperform the caches that the OS is already providing.\r\n\r\nI think there may be an interesting discussion we could have in the future with regards to some modules which are a bit slower (I'm thinking the git modules and the toolchain modules which show version info). When running `startship init` we could launch a daemon which watches relevant files in your recent/most-used directories, and pre-calculates and caches your prompt so we can display it near-instantly.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
